<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayakeshi I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1050–1080</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayakeshi I was a king of the Kadamba dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a> in the 11th century, ruling as a feudatory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a>. He moved the Kadamba capital from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandor">Chandrapura</a> to the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa-velha">Gopakapattana</a> on the Zuari river, which grew into a busy harbour trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. His reign marked the high point of Kadamba power on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a>.</p></div>
